\title{Invertible / bijective}
\date{2026-03-10T11:22:38Z}
\tag{discrete}

\import{discrete-macros}

\taxon{Definition}
\p{A function #{f : A \to B} which is both [one-to-one](00A0) and [onto](00A8) (injective and surjective) is called \em{invertible} (\em{bijective}, a \em{bijection}). We write #{f^{-1} : B \to A} for the \em{inverse} of #{f}, that is, the function defined by #{f^{-1}(b) = a} if and only if #{f(a) = b}.}

